#! Rename (s133), under the fackr profile: `prepareRename` answers the
#! token and placeholder; `rename` answers the whole edit — the use in
#! the entry AND the declaration in the sibling the client never opened —
#! as `documentChanges` where the client declares it and the `changes`
#! map where it does not. Then the refusal set, by name, each a
#! `RequestFailed` ResponseError and never a partial edit: a prelude name
#! (`print`), a module (`geometry`, a directory), a keyword position
#! (`fn`), and a new name that is a keyword. A local renames in one file.
name      navigation/rename-fackr
profile   fackr

initialize
open      resolve/two_mod/main.lu
wait      diagnostics resolve/two_mod/main.lu
req       prepareRename resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:16
req       rename resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:16 square
req       rename resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:7 geo
req       rename resolve/two_mod/main.lu 10:0 g
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
req       prepareRename hello.lu 10:4
req       rename hello.lu 10:4 say
req       rename hello.lu 10:19 let
req       rename hello.lu 10:19 whom
shutdown
